// Step 3 - value shape: decide the aggregation per metric before drawing anything.
// Observed with Application Insights Java 3.7.10:
// - Counter: every row has valueCount = 1 and value = the increment of one 60 s step (sum it).
// - DistributionSummary/Timer: valueCount = recordings in the step and valueSum = their total
//   (sum(valueSum) / sum(valueCount) = average). A rarely used one can also show valueCount = 1,
//   so maxValueCount = 1 alone does not prove a Counter; confirm with the meter type in code.
// - Gauge: value is a point-in-time level (do not sum over time).
customMetrics
| where timestamp > ago(30m)
| where name startswith "movielog_"
| where isnotempty(cloud_RoleInstance)
| summarize rows = count(), instances = dcount(cloud_RoleInstance),
            maxValueCount = max(valueCount),
            minValue = min(value), maxValue = max(value),
            sumValueSum = sum(valueSum), sumValueCount = sum(valueCount)
    by name
| extend rowsPerInstancePerMin = round(rows * 1.0 / instances / 30, 2)
| project name, rows, instances, rowsPerInstancePerMin, maxValueCount, minValue, maxValue, sumValueSum, sumValueCount
| order by name asc
